basalt-security: TPM2 disk unlock and Secure Boot helpers for Basalt OS.

  basalt-tpm status | pcrs | reenroll | suspend
  basalt-secureboot status | enroll-mok | unenroll-mok

basalt-tpm-resume.service re-seals the TPM2 key on the boot after
`basalt-tpm suspend`. basalt-module-keys.service loads the Basalt module
signing certificates into the kernel's secondary trusted keyring at boot;
they are accepted when the Basalt module CA is enrolled as a MOK.

Design and procedures: docs/secure-boot.md in the Basalt OS repository,
https://github.com/basalt-os/basalt-os
